  "about": "Strings as DataOutputStream.writeUTF writes them (Java's modified UTF-8: a two-byte big-endian length, NUL as C0 80, every UTF-16 code unit on its own, so a surrogate pair is two three-byte groups and a lone surrogate is kept), and as String.toByteArray() writes them (standard UTF-8; a lone surrogate becomes '?'). The sync wire uses writeUTF for every string and toByteArray for the JSON of the data.",
